--TEST--
`Core\Test::request` runs a request through the compiled route table in this process, so the program answering it reads the match the door took — `rule:testing/in-process-request`, ADR 0102 § 1
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 18's first mechanism: no socket and no port, and the table it matches
// against is the one this file's own `#[Route]` declarations compiled to. What
// is asserted is that the *match* crossed -- the child reads
// `Core\Request::route()` and finds the row named below, which is the whole of
// "dispatches through the compiled route table". Nothing here dispatches: ADR
// 0102 § 1 leaves what a match means to the program, and the program is the
// `else` branch below.
//
// **The branch is the request, and the `catch` is how a case tells the two
// sides apart.** The program answering an in-process request is this same
// program -- its script frame is what a served request runs -- so the child
// reaches the same `Core\Test::request` call and is refused: an in-process
// request may not be made from inside one (`nvs_runtime::inproc`). That
// refusal is what makes a one-file case possible at all, and it is a rule
// rather than a trick, since without it a program with a top-level request
// would answer its own request forever.
class Api {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/users/1", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "Api::show")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function show(): string { return "shown"; }
}

try {
    var $answered = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/users/1");
    echo "status ", $answered->status(), "\n";
    echo "body ", $answered->body(), "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
    // The child. `route()` is the match the caller took before this isolate
    // existed, which is ADR 0102 § 1's "once, before any application code
    // runs" holding for a synthetic request exactly as it does for an arrived
    // one.
    var $matched = Core\Request::route();
    if ($matched == null) {
        echo "the table claimed nothing";
    } else {
        echo $matched->name() ?? "unnamed";
    }
}
--EXPECT--
status 200
body Api::show
